<http://data.silknow.org/object/4dd9a9d9-2699-3f6a-874f-911464744999/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Woman's petticoat made of light blue silk satin lined with glazed undyed wool and wadded with a thin layer of wool.  It is quilted in running stitch with light blue silk thread in a border of flowers and leaves at the hem and undulating parallel diagonal lines above.  The petticoat is made of 6 panels of silk, with pocket openings in the side seams.  There is a wide box pleat, with side pleats, at the centre front, and an inverted box pleat, with side pleats at centre back.  The waist is bound with a ⅞-inch (2.2 cm) wide blue linen tape, extending to form the ties on each side."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/4dd9a9d9-2699-3f6a-874f-911464744999> .

